sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/aristotle-pa02-31> a delphi:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Some animals close the eye with the lower lid; birds blink with a membrane" ;
    dct:description "Viviparous animals have two eyelids and use both to close and to blink; oviparous quadrupeds and heavy-bodied birds close the eye with the lower lid only, while birds blink with a membrane issuing from the corner of the eye." ;
    delphi:context "Aristotle, On the Parts of Animals (De Partibus Animalium), Book II, Part 13; translated by William Ogle, The Works of Aristotle Translated into English, ed. J. A. Smith and W. D. Ross, Oxford: Clarendon Press, vol. V (1912). Scope: viviparous animals (mammals), oviparous quadrupeds (reptiles), heavy-bodied birds (e.g. fowl) and birds generally" ;
    dct:type "empirical-generalization" .
}

